  "body": "Docs for the camcraft-mcp skill (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`), the rest of #1013 after PR #1024 (`Refs #1013`) landed the first two drawn-cutter rows.\n\nRows as added or changed:\n\n- Added `set_tool_cutter_params { \"tool\": string, \"params\"?: {diameter?, corner_r?, tip_angle?, flute_len?, shank_d?, shank_len?}, \"neck\"?: {diameter, length} | null }` after `set_tool_cutter_profile`. Its parameter shape and behaviour come from `crates/app/src/mcp/cutter_tools.rs` on upstream main (`s_params`, its description): numbers in mm, `tip_angle` in degrees, any subset; a drawn outline is carried onto the new numbers; `neck` draws a straight neck, `null` drops the drawn outline, omitted keeps it; one undo step; refusals by name.\n- Changed `set_tool_cutter_profile`: \"Display only: toolpaths and checks keep reading the numbers.\" is replaced with \"Toolpaths keep reading the numbers; the collision checks and the simulation read a drawn neck where it is narrower than the stated shank (never wider).\" (#957).\n\nPinning test: none. Docs only; `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main --dry-run` plans no crate tests (only the skill file and PROCESS_VERSION changed).\n\nNot exercised: the skill rows were not run against a live MCP server; they were checked against the schema and description in `cutter_tools.rs`.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0.\n\nPROCESS_VERSION 35 · PR #1309 · camcraft-mcp skill lists set_tool_cutter_params · a fork must: pull the process files\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1013\n\n",
